# policy_bw run matrix  (read by scripts/launch.sh)
#
# Declares the co-location runs for the POLICY (action-distribution) attack. When
# this file is present, launch.sh ignores its default layout and builds the matrix
# below: one victim trace on core 0, co-located against each NEIGHBOR trace on
# core 1, crossed with each CONFIG.
#
# Columns are whitespace-separated. Lines starting with '#' and blanks ignored.
#
#   victim   <source>                 [prog-args...]
#   neighbor <name> <source>          [prog-args...]
#   config   <name> <ini>
#
# <source> is resolved relative to this attack dir first, then codes/.
# Trace args (idle/light/...) are passed to the workload under PIN, so one source
# (attacker.c) yields several neighbor traces by argument alone.
# Output .out files are named <neighbor>_<config>.out (consumed by rollup.py).

victim   victim.c

neighbor atk_idle      attacker.c      idle
neighbor atk_light     attacker.c      light
neighbor atk_medium    attacker.c      medium
neighbor atk_heavy     attacker.c      heavy

# aware = HBW reward table live (attack); blind = reward table inert (isolation).
# Both pin the HBW degree curve EQUAL to normal, so the degree lever is off and
# any policy movement is reward-shaping alone.
config   aware   aware.ini
config   blind   blind.ini
